XB-Kidux-Name-en: CodeCombat
XB-Kidux-Description-en: The CodeCombat website, where you learn Python and JavaScript by playing. It needs the internet and a CodeCombat account, paid for most of it; Kidux is not connected with CodeCombat.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: CodeCombat
XB-Kidux-Description-es: La web de CodeCombat, donde se aprende Python y JavaScript jugando. Necesita internet y una cuenta de CodeCombat, de pago para casi todo; Kidux no tiene ninguna relación con CodeCombat.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 9-16
XB-Kidux-Before: scratch
Description: Kidux learning module: CodeCombat, a door to the CodeCombat website
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module opens the CodeCombat website, where children learn Python and
 JavaScript by playing, in a window of its own, and no other website: a
 link to anywhere else leads nowhere. Nothing of CodeCombat is in this
 package; the site, its levels and its accounts are CodeCombat's.
 .
 It needs the internet and a CodeCombat account, and most of the site
 needs a paid subscription, which an adult buys on another computer. The
 child signs in with an email address and a password; signing in through
 Google, Facebook or Clever does not work here.
 .
 Kidux and its author have no connection with CodeCombat Inc.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
